WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:03.690
Let's say that you
started off with 3 apples.

00:03.690 --> 00:09.680
And then I were to give you
another 7, another 7 apples.

00:09.680 --> 00:13.030
So my question to you-- and
this might be very obvious--

00:13.030 --> 00:17.930
is how many apples
do you now have?

00:17.930 --> 00:21.910
And I'll give you a second
to think about that.

00:21.910 --> 00:23.420
Well, this is fairly basic.

00:23.420 --> 00:24.344
You had 3 apples.

00:24.344 --> 00:25.760
Now, I'm going to
give you 7 more.

00:25.760 --> 00:27.370
You now have 3 plus 7.

00:27.370 --> 00:30.030
You now have 10 apples.

00:30.030 --> 00:32.770
But let's say I want to do
the same type of thinking,

00:32.770 --> 00:35.352
but I'm too lazy to
write the word "apples."

00:35.352 --> 00:37.310
Let's say instead of
writing the word "apples,"

00:37.310 --> 00:39.840
I just use the letter a.

00:39.840 --> 00:42.330
And let's say this is,
say, a different scenario.

00:42.330 --> 00:46.450
You start off with 4 apples.

00:46.450 --> 00:51.220
And to that, I add
another 2 apples.

00:51.220 --> 00:53.570
How many apples do you now have?

00:53.570 --> 00:56.650
Instead of writing apples, I'm
just going to write a's here.

00:56.650 --> 00:59.260
So how many of these
a's do you now have?

00:59.260 --> 01:01.320
And once again, I'll
give you a few seconds

01:01.320 --> 01:04.819
to think about that.

01:04.819 --> 01:07.200
This also might be a little
bit of common sense for you.

01:07.200 --> 01:10.960
If you had 4 of these apples or
whatever these a's represented,

01:10.960 --> 01:13.220
if you had 4 of them and
then you add 2 more of them,

01:13.220 --> 01:16.410
you're now going to
have 6 of these apples.

01:16.410 --> 01:18.660
But once again, we
started off assuming

01:18.660 --> 01:20.180
that a's represent apples.

01:20.180 --> 01:22.140
But they could have
represented anything.

01:22.140 --> 01:25.030
If you have 4 of whatever
a represents, and then you

01:25.030 --> 01:27.670
have another 2 of
whatever a represents,

01:27.670 --> 01:29.980
you'll now have 6 of
whatever a represents.

01:29.980 --> 01:32.896
Or if you just think of it if
I have 4 a's, and then I add

01:32.896 --> 01:34.520
another 2 a's, I'm
going to have 6 a's.

01:34.520 --> 01:40.490
You can literally think of 4
a's as a plus a plus a plus a.

01:40.490 --> 01:45.320
And if to that, I add another
2 a's-- so plus a plus

01:45.320 --> 01:47.310
a, that's 2 a's
right over there--

01:47.310 --> 01:49.030
how many a's do I now have?

01:49.030 --> 01:52.400
Well, that's 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6.

01:52.400 --> 01:55.717
I now have 6 a's.

01:55.717 --> 01:57.800
So thinking of it that
way, let's get a little bit

01:57.800 --> 02:00.210
more abstract.

02:00.210 --> 02:04.840
Let's say that I have 5
x's, whatever x represents.

02:04.840 --> 02:06.510
x could be some number.

02:06.510 --> 02:08.940
So I have 5 of whatever
that number is.

02:08.940 --> 02:14.590
And from that, I subtract 2
of whatever that number is.

02:14.590 --> 02:16.310
What would this evaluate to?

02:16.310 --> 02:22.110
How many of these
x's would I now have?

02:22.110 --> 02:27.760
So it's essentially 5x minus
2x is going to be what times x?

02:27.760 --> 02:30.280
Once again, I'll give you a
few seconds to think about it.

02:33.050 --> 02:36.350
Well, if I have 5 of something
and I subtract 2 of those away,

02:36.350 --> 02:39.050
I'm going to have 3 of
that something left.

02:39.050 --> 02:41.720
So this is going
to be equal to 3x.

02:41.720 --> 02:44.984
5x minus 2x is equal to 3x.

02:44.984 --> 02:46.900
And if you really think
about what that means,

02:46.900 --> 02:52.490
five x's are just x plus
x plus x plus x plus x.

02:52.490 --> 02:56.900
And then we're going to
take away two of those x's.

02:56.900 --> 03:00.490
So take away one x,
take away two x's.

03:00.490 --> 03:05.328
You are going to be
left with three x's.
